- op: discuss  # 6686
  at: '2026-07-02T16:29:58Z'  # 6686
  by: agent  # 6686
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6686
  clock: 3  # 6686
  nonce: '6686'  # 6686
  message: "Done via PR #385 (merged FF). _process_call's terminal bare-Name call branch now emits a calls edge python:builtins:0-0:open:unresolved (dst_ref module=builtins) for bare builtin I/O constructors (open) via EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES — the io_primitives/python.yaml builtins rows (fs_read/fs_write functions=[open]) were dead (no edge targeted them). Behavioral evidence (production-path extract_nodes, the item's filed repro): a module with open() in assign / with / chained-.read() / return forms now yields exactly 1 calls edge to python:builtins:0-0:open:unresolved per call (was 0 in every form). Orthogonal to WI-fuvuj's receiver .read()/.write() edges (module=file). core+mainstream 100% coverage in isolation; CI passed. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: adds an edge on every Python open() call corpus-wide (edge / io-boundary / dead-code counts shift)."  # 6686
